.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EC_KEY_GET_ENC_FLAGS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EC_KEY_get_enc_flags ,
.Nm EC_KEY_set_enc_flags
.Nd Get and set flags for encoding EC_KEY structures
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ec.h
.Ft unsigned int
.Fo EC_KEY_get_enc_flags
.Fa "const EC_KEY *key"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo EC_KEY_set_enc_flags
.Fa "EC_KEY *eckey"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The format of the external representation of the public key written by
.Xr i2d_ECPrivateKey 3
(such as whether it is stored in a compressed form or not) is described
by the point_conversion_form.
See
.Xr EC_GROUP_copy 3
for a description of point_conversion_form.
.Pp
When reading a private key encoded without an associated public key
(e.g.
if EC_PKEY_NO_PUBKEY has been used - see below), then
.Xr d2i_ECPrivateKey 3
generates the missing public key automatically.
Private keys encoded without parameters (e.g.
if EC_PKEY_NO_PARAMETERS has been used - see below) cannot be loaded
using
.Xr d2i_ECPrivateKey 3 .
.Pp
The functions
.Fn EC_KEY_get_enc_flags
and
.Fn EC_KEY_set_enc_flags
get and set the value of the encoding flags for the
.Fa key .
There are two encoding flags currently defined - EC_PKEY_NO_PARAMETERS
and EC_PKEY_NO_PUBKEY. These flags define the behaviour of how the
.Fa key
is converted into ASN1 in a call to
.Xr i2d_ECPrivateKey 3 .
If EC_PKEY_NO_PARAMETERS is set then the public parameters for the curve
are not encoded along with the private key.
If EC_PKEY_NO_PUBKEY is set then the public key is not encoded along
with the private key.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EC_KEY_get_enc_flags
returns the value of the current encoding flags for the EC_KEY.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crypto 7 ,
.Xr EC_GROUP_new 3 ,
.Xr EC_GROUP_copy 3 ,
.Xr EC_POINT_new 3 ,
.Xr EC_POINT_add 3 ,
.Xr EC_GFp_simple_method 3 ,
.Xr d2i_ECPKParameters 3 ,
.Xr d2i_ECPrivateKey 3
